  "notes": [
    "VCC is pin 3 and GND is pin 12. The LM324 in the same package uses pins 4 and 11. Dropping an LM339 into an LM324 socket connects power to two inputs.",
    "All four outputs are open collector and do nothing without a pull-up. Tie several together on one pull-up for a wired-AND, which is how multi-channel fault detectors are built.",
    "With no hysteresis a slow input chatters. Add positive feedback from output to the non-inverting input, a few hundred k, for a Schmitt trigger. Nearly every real circuit needs it.",
    "Two comparators plus one AND gate gives you a window comparator, which is the classic use for a quad part.",
    "Input common mode goes to ground but stops about 1.5 V below V+, same as the LM393 and LM324.",
    "The LM393 is two of these in a DIP-8 with the same arrangement as the LM358."
  ],
